(MOMENTUM STRATEGIES IN A MODERN U.S. EQUITY SAMPLE) Tj
T*
(Replication of Jegadeesh and Titman \(1993\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Research question) Tj
T*
(Do stocks with strong past returns continue to outperform stocks with weak past) Tj
T*
(returns? This project applies a market-model approach to monthly momentum portfolios) Tj
T*
(and examines whether winner-minus-loser returns vary with firm size.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Data and sample) Tj
T*
(The current analysis covers December 2001 through December 2025, a modern sample) Tj
T*
(period used in the course brief. The analysis-ready inputs contain monthly returns) Tj
T*
(for decile portfolios P1-P10, the winner-minus-loser spread \(WML\), a market return,) Tj
T*
(and the monthly risk-free rate. Size-sorted results are available for small, medium,) Tj
T*
(and large firms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is a modern-sample application of the paper's method, not an exact numerical) Tj
T*
(replication of the original historical sample. Licensed course/CRSP source data are) Tj
T*
(not published in this repository. Users must obtain authorized inputs through the) Tj
T*
(course and construct the documented local analysis files.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Empirical design) Tj
T*
(For each decile portfolio, estimate:) Tj
T*
(Rp,t - RF,t = alpha_p + beta_p \(Rm,t - RF,t\) + error_p,t.) Tj
T*
(For WML, regress the winner-minus-loser spread on market excess return. Do not) Tj
T*
(subtract RF from WML a second time because WML is already a long-short spread.) Tj
T*
(Use Newey-West/HAC standard errors with five lags.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Core replication results) Tj
T*
(The currently checked Stata estimates show a full-sample WML alpha of 0.011317 per) Tj
T*
(month \(about 1.132 percent per month\), with a HAC t-statistic of 2.94. This is) Tj
T*
(statistically significant at the 1 percent level using conventional two-sided) Tj
T*
(critical values and indicates a positive market-adjusted momentum spread.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The loser portfolio P1 has alpha -0.01035 per month \(t = -2.22\), significant at the) Tj
T*
(5 percent level. The winner portfolio P10 has alpha 0.000966 \(t = 0.44\), which is) Tj
T*
(not statistically significant. The full-sample pattern is therefore more clearly) Tj
T*
(associated with a negative alpha for losers than a statistically significant) Tj
T*
(positive alpha for winners.) Tj
ET
endstream
