(5. Results by firm size) Tj
T*
(The WML market-model estimates by size group are:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Sample       Monthly alpha       HAC t-statistic) Tj
T*
(Small        0.014671 \(1.467%\)    3.11) Tj
T*
(Medium       0.010555 \(1.056%\)    3.04) Tj
T*
(Large        0.007460 \(0.746%\)    2.65) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(All three estimates are positive and statistically significant at approximately) Tj
T*
(the 1 percent level. The point estimate is largest among small firms and declines) Tj
T*
(across medium- and large-size groups. This pattern is consistent with stronger) Tj
T*
(momentum among smaller firms, but the ordering of point estimates alone does not) Tj
T*
(show that the differences are statistically significant.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Independent extension: size heterogeneity) Tj
T*
(The extension formally tests pairwise differences in size-group WML alphas. For) Tj
T*
(each pair, estimate the intercept in a time-series regression of the difference) Tj
T*
(between the two groups' WML returns on market excess return, using HAC standard) Tj
T*
(errors with five lags. The intercept estimates the difference in their market-model) Tj
T*
(alphas under a common time index.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The extension output must be generated by running code/run_all.py with the approved) Tj
T*
(local input files. Its pairwise estimates and t-statistics have not yet been checked) Tj
T*
(against those files, so no conclusion about statistically significant cross-size) Tj
T*
(differences is made in this draft.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Comparison with the original paper) Tj
T*
(The positive WML spread is qualitatively consistent with the broad momentum finding) Tj
T*
(of Jegadeesh and Titman \(1993\). Exact numerical equality is not expected because) Tj
T*
(this project uses a modern 2001-2025 sample rather than the original paper's) Tj
T*
(historical period. Data coverage and implementation choices may also differ.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Validation, limitations, and conclusion) Tj
T*
(Before submission, verify monthly date alignment, return units, missing observations,) Tj
T*
(the market and risk-free-rate merges, and the construction WML = P10 - P1. Compare) Tj
T*
(Python outputs with independent Stata estimates. The reported core estimates provide) Tj
T*
(evidence of a positive market-adjusted momentum spread in the modern sample, with) Tj
T*
(positive point estimates in all size groups. The formal extension must be run before) Tj
T*
(concluding whether size-group alphas differ statistically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(References) Tj
T*
(Jegadeesh, N., and S. Titman \(1993\). Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers:) Tj
T*
(Implications for Stock Market Efficiency. The Journal of Finance, 48\(1\), 65-91.) Tj
T*
(DOI: 10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Draft status: this PDF summarizes currently checked Stata core results. Update it) Tj
T*
(after the Python workflow has been run on the approved inputs and all extension) Tj
T*
(results and figures have been independently validated.) Tj
ET
